4:["$","p",null,{"className":"text-base sm:text-lg text-white/70 max-w-xl mx-auto mb-6","children":"SPH, CYL, AXIS, ADD -- your prescription card can look like a foreign language. This plain-English guide decodes every number and abbreviation."}]
5:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center justify-center gap-4 text-sm text-white/50","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-1.5","children":[["$","svg",null,{"className":"w-4 h-4","fill":"none","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","children":["$","path",null,{"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","d":"M6.75 3v2.25M17.25 3v2.25M3 18.75V7.5a2.25 2.25 0 012.25-2.25h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0121 7.5v11.25m-18 0A2.25 2.25 0 005.25 21h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0021 18.75m-18 0v-7.5A2.25 2.25 0 015.25 9h13.5A2.25 2.25 0 0121 11.25v7.5"}]}],"20 July 2025"]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"w-px h-3.5 bg-white/20"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-1.5","children":[["$","svg",null,{"className":"w-4 h-4","fill":"none","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","children":["$","path",null,{"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","d":"M12 6v6h4.5m4.5 0a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"}]}],"8 min read"]}]]}]
6:["$","section",null,{"className":"py-12 sm:py-16","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"lg:col-span-2","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"relative aspect-[16/9] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden mb-8","children":["$","$Lc",null,{"src":"/images/retinal-scan-sm.jpg","alt":"Understanding Your Eye Test Results & Prescription","fill":true,"sizes":"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 66vw","className":"object-cover","priority":true}]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"prose prose-gray max-w-none","children":[["$","h2","0",{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-navy)] mt-10 mb-4","style":{"fontFamily":"var(--font-display)"},"children":"Why it pays to understand your prescription"}],["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-5","children":"After every eye test, you are legally entitled to receive a copy of your optical prescription. This small card or slip of paper contains all the information needed to make your glasses or order contact lenses, and it belongs to you regardless of where you choose to buy your eyewear. Yet for many people, the prescription is a bewildering string of numbers, abbreviations, and symbols that might as well be written in code."}],["$","p","2",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-5","children":"Understanding what your prescription means empowers you to make informed decisions about your eye care. You can compare prices confidently, order glasses online with peace of mind, check that your lenses have been made correctly, and track how your vision changes over time. It also helps you have more meaningful conversations with your optometrist and ask the right questions about your eye health."}],["$","p","3",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-5","children":"This guide will walk you through every element of a standard UK optical prescription, explain what each number means in practical terms, and give you the confidence to read and interpret your own results."}],["$","h2","4",{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-navy)] mt-10 mb-4","style":{"fontFamily":"var(--font-display)"},"children":"The layout of a prescription"}],["$","p","5",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-5","children":"A UK optical prescription is typically presented in a table format with separate rows for each eye. The right eye is labelled \"R\" or \"RE\" (sometimes \"OD,\" from the Latin oculus dexter), and the left eye is labelled \"L\" or \"LE\" (sometimes \"OS,\" from oculus sinister). If a measurement applies to both eyes together, it may be labelled \"OU\" (oculi uterque)."}],["$","p","6",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-5","children":"The main columns you will encounter are SPH (sphere), CYL (cylinder), AXIS, and ADD (addition). Some prescriptions also include a PRISM value and a BASE direction, though these are less common. Each of these measurements is expressed in dioptres (abbreviated \"D\" or \"DS\"), which is the unit used to describe the optical power of a lens. Let us look at each one in detail."}],["$","h2","7",{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-navy)] mt-10 mb-4","style":{"fontFamily":"var(--font-display)"},"children":"SPH — the sphere value"}],["$","p","8",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-5","children":"The sphere value indicates the main focusing power of the lens needed to correct your distance vision. It tells you whether you are short-sighted (myopic) or long-sighted (hypermetropic), and by how much."}],"$Ld","$Le","$Lf","$L10","$L11","$L12","$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27"]}]]}],"$L28"]}]}]}]
7:["$","section",null,{"className":"py-16 sm:py-20 bg-gray-50","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-center mb-12","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--color-navy)] mb-3","style":{"fontFamily":"var(--font-display)"},"children":"More articles"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-500 max-w-lg mx-auto","children":"Continue reading our expert guides on eye tests and eye health"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 lg:gap-8","children":[["$","$L3","how-often-should-you-have-an-eye-test",{"href":"/articles/how-often-should-you-have-an-eye-test","className":"group card-lift flex flex-col bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 shadow-sm overflow-hidden h-full","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"relative aspect-[16/10] img-zoom","children":[["$","$Lc",null,{"src":"/images/optician-shop-sm.jpg","alt":"How Often Should You Have an Eye Test? — Age-by-Age Advice","fill":true,"sizes":"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 33vw","className":"object-cover"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"absolute top-3 left-3 text-xs font-medium px-3 py-1 rounded-full backdrop-blur-sm bg-[var(--color-primary)]/10 text-[var(--color-primary)]","children":"Eye Health"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col flex-1 p-5 sm:p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-[var(--color-navy)] group-hover:text-[var(--color-primary)] transition-colors mb-2 line-clamp-2","style":{"fontFamily":"var(--font-display)"},"children":"How Often Should You Have an Eye Test? — Age-by-Age Advice"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-4 line-clamp-3","children":"From toddlers to over-70s, the recommended frequency of eye tests varies by age, health, and risk factors. Learn exactly when to book your next appointment."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-auto flex items-center justify-between","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-gray-400","children":"7 min read"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-primary)] group-hover:gap-2 transition-all","children":["Read more",["$","svg",null,{"className":"w-4 h-4","fill":"none","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","children":["$","path",null,{"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","d":"M9 5l7 7-7 7"}]}]]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","$L3","what-happens-during-an-eye-test",{"href":"/articles/what-happens-during-an-eye-test","className":"group card-lift flex flex-col bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 shadow-sm overflow-hidden h-full","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"relative aspect-[16/10] img-zoom","children":[["$","$Lc",null,{"src":"/images/eye-test-phoropter-sm.jpg","alt":"What Happens During an Eye Test? A Step-by-Step Guide","fill":true,"sizes":"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 33vw","className":"object-cover"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"absolute top-3 left-3 text-xs font-medium px-3 py-1 rounded-full backdrop-blur-sm bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700","children":"Guides"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col flex-1 p-5 sm:p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-[var(--color-navy)] group-hover:text-[var(--color-primary)] transition-colors mb-2 line-clamp-2","style":{"fontFamily":"var(--font-display)"},"children":"What Happens During an Eye Test? A Step-by-Step Guide"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-4 line-clamp-3","children":"Nervous about your eye test? Walk through every stage of a modern UK eye examination, from the history questions to the final prescription."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-auto flex items-center justify-between","children":["$L29","$L2a"]}]]}]]}],"$L2b","$L2c","$L2d"]}]]}]}]
8:["$","section",null,{"className":"py-16 sm:py-20 bg-[var(--color-navy)]","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 text-center","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-4","style":{"fontFamily":"var(--font-display)"},"children":"Protect your vision with a regular eye test"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-white/70 mb-8 max-w-lg mx-auto","children":"Regular eye tests are the best way to detect problems early. Compare opticians and book online for free."}],["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/search","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-[var(--color-primary)] hover:bg-[var(--color-primary-dark)] text-white font-semibold text-base px-8 py-4 rounded-full transition-all hover:shadow-lg","children":[["$","svg",null,{"className":"w-5 h-5","fill":"none","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2.5","children":["$","path",null,{"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","d":"M21 21l-6-6m2-5a7 7 0 11-14 0 7 7 0 0114 0z"}]}],"Book an Eye Test"]}]]}]}]
9:["$","footer",null,{"className":"bg-[var(--color-navy)] text-white","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 sm:py-16","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-8 mb-12","children":[["$","div","Eye Tests",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-white/80 uppercase tracking-wider mb-4","children":"Eye Tests"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-2","children":[["$","li","Standard Eye Test",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/eye-tests/standard-eye-test","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"Standard Eye Test"}]}],["$","li","NHS Eye Test",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/eye-tests/nhs-eye-test","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"NHS Eye Test"}]}],["$","li","Children's Eye Test",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/eye-tests/childrens-eye-test","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"Children's Eye Test"}]}],["$","li","Contact Lens Fitting",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/eye-tests/contact-lens-fitting","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"Contact Lens Fitting"}]}],["$","li","OCT Scan",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/eye-tests/oct-scan","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"OCT Scan"}]}],["$","li","Visual Field Test",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/eye-tests/visual-field-test","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"Visual Field Test"}]}],["$","li","Diabetic Eye Screening",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/eye-tests/diabetic-eye-screening","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"Diabetic Eye Screening"}]}],["$","li","Dry Eye Assessment",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/eye-tests/dry-eye-assessment","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"Dry Eye Assessment"}]}],["$","li","DVLA / Driving Test",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/eye-tests/dvla-driving-vision-test","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"DVLA / Driving Test"}]}],["$","li","At-Home Eye Tests",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/at-home-eye-tests","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"At-Home Eye Tests"}]}],["$","li","View All Eye Tests",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/eye-tests","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"View All Eye Tests"}]}]]}]]}],["$","div","Opticians",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-white/80 uppercase tracking-wider mb-4","children":"Opticians"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-2","children":[["$","li","Boots Opticians",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/opticians/boots-opticians","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"Boots Opticians"}]}],["$","li","ASDA Opticians",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/opticians/asda-opticians","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"ASDA Opticians"}]}],["$","li","M&S Opticians",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/opticians/mands-opticians","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"M&S Opticians"}]}],["$","li","Ace & Tate",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/opticians/ace-and-tate","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"Ace & Tate"}]}],["$","li","Leightons",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/opticians/leightons","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"Leightons"}]}],["$","li","Rawlings",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/opticians/rawlings","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"Rawlings"}]}],["$","li","Scrivens",{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/opticians/scrivens","className":"text-sm text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors","children":"Scrivens"}]}],"$L2e","$L2f","$L30"]}]]}],"$L31","$L32","$L33"]}]}],"$L34","$L35","$L36"]}]
